{"toolCallId":"call_24024fd72a664c9aa16ce365efb3f323","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"=== AC metadata example ===\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n**Packet:** sk-git/033-git-setup-customization/005-setup-check-hardening\n**Level:** 2\n**Status:** In Progress\n**Date:** 2026-10-15\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:criteria -->\n## 2. CRITERIA\n\nOne row per criterion. `AC-ID` is stable once written: supersede a criterion, never renumber it.\n\n| AC-ID | REQ | Given / When / Then | Verification | Status | Waiver |\n|-------|-----|---------------------|--------------|--------|--------|\n| AC-001 | REQ-001 | Given a fixture whose `hook-flags.env` sets `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=1` and an environment without it, When the battery runs, Then the suppression row is FAIL, lists the value with the file as its source and names the file line in its repair | The T005 test, plus its mutation check. Observed: \"a master switch saved in hook-flags.env fails suppression and names its line\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs:505`) passes, and the old `checkSuppression` restored made 3 tests fail | Met | - |\n| AC-002 | REQ-001 | Given the same file and `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED=` set empty in the environment, When the battery runs, Then the suppression row is PASS, because the environment wins as `hook-flags.cjs:160-163` does | The T005 empty-override test. Observed: the same test sets `SYSTEM_HOOKS_DISABLED` to an empty string and asserts PASS (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs:517`) | Met | - |\n| AC-003 | REQ-002 | Given a `.codex/hooks.json` that names the advisory only under `SessionStart`, When the battery runs with `--tool codex`, Then the ai-tool-hooks row is FAIL, and the same holds for a wrong event or a non-matching matcher under Claude, Devin and Cursor | The T006 negative tests, plus its mutation check. Observed: \"ai-tool-hooks accepts each runtime's real wiring and refuses a wrong event or matcher\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs:836`) fails each runtime under a wrong event and a wrong matcher. The old substring match failed it at the wrong event, and a matcher check forced true failed it at the Claude matcher case | Met | - |\n| AC-004 | REQ-002 | Given copies of this checkout's four real adapter configs, When the battery runs with each tool, Then each is reported registered, and the hooks README section 3 rows show the same matchers | The T006 real-shape tests and the T007 diff. Observed: the same test passes copies of this checkout's Claude, Codex, Devin and Cursor configs (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs:836`), and `.skilled/skills/sk-git/scripts/hooks/README.md:77-78` show matcher `Bash` and matcher `exec\\|Bash` | Met | - |\n| AC-005 | REQ-003 | Given each of the six status-matrix rows from `plan.md`, When the battery runs in human and JSON mode, Then the STATUS line, the JSON `status` and the exit code are OK with 0, DEGRADED with 3 or FAIL with 1 as the matrix says, and a usage error still exits 2 | The T004 matrix tests. Observed: \"the status fold maps rows to OK 0, DEGRADED 3 and FAIL 1 in both modes\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs:241`) runs six cases in human and JSON mode, and the non-repository test (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs:271`) still exits 2 | Met | - |\n| AC-006 | REQ-003 | Given the docs that state the exit codes, When they are searched for `STATUS=` and exit codes, Then each shows 0, 1, 2 and 3 and the three STATUS lines | `rg` over the consumer list in `plan.md` after T026 to T029. Observed: `doctor-git-setup.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-git-presentation.txt:256`, DOC-384 lines 26 to 30, the playbook line 947, the catalog leaf line 29 and `README.md:1505` each state 0, 3, 1 and 2, and the presentation and README show the three STATUS lines | Met | - |\n| AC-007 | REQ-004 | Given a gate helper that prints a report without `gates`, one that exits nonzero and a parent `GATE_REGISTRY` pointing at a stub, When the battery runs, Then the gates row is UNKNOWN with no repair for the first two and the stub is never read | The T008 tests. Observed: \"gates reports UNKNOWN with no repair when the helper fails or its report has no gates\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs:933`) and \"gates ignores a GATE_REGISTRY inherited from the environment\" (`.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/git-setup-check.test.cjs:980`), each failed by its mutation | Met | - |\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"cdf913","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_29cef6f2e61249c19715648fc1ffb5fe","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"Files /tmp/speckit-before/graph-metadata.json and specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/graph-metadata.json differ\nFiles /tmp/speckit-before/implementation-summary.md and specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md differ\n=== pointer lines now ===\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md:10:    packet_pointer: \"zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\"\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:10:    packet_pointer: \"scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\"\n=== causal summary now ===\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/description.json:3:  \"description\": \"Add a quiet flag to recommend-level.sh\",\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/graph-metadata.json:192:    \"causal_summary\": \"Callers that need only the level must parse a 16-line report to read one number\",\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"1841a0","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_2c006394378a47d8b5191c5b58577ecd","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# COMPONENT: CHECK-SCAFFOLD-NEVER-TOUCHED\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n# Sourced by validate.sh and compatible with strict mode.\nset -euo pipefail\n\n_scaffold_rule_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\n# shellcheck source=../lib/status-classifier.sh\nsource \"${_scaffold_rule_dir}/../lib/status-classifier.sh\"\n\n# Rule: SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED\n# Severity: error\n# Description: Detects scaffold-origin docs whose folder claims Complete status.\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 1. INITIALIZATION\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nrun_check() {\n    local folder=\"$1\"\n    local level=\"$2\"\n    : \"$level\"\n\n    RULE_NAME=\"SCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED\"\n    RULE_STATUS=\"pass\"\n    RULE_MESSAGE=\"\"\n    RULE_DETAILS=()\n    RULE_REMEDIATION=\"\"\n\n    local spec_file=\"$folder/spec.md\"\n    local status_value=\"\"\n    local spec_complete=false\n    local -a files=(\"plan.md\" \"tasks.md\" \"implementation-summary.md\")\n    local -a found_markers=()\n\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# 2. VALIDATION LOGIC\n# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n    status_value=\"$(extract_status_table_value \"$spec_file\")\"\n\n    if [[ \"$(classify_status \"$status_value\")\" == \"complete\" ]]; then\n        spec_complete=true\n    fi\n\n    if [[ \"$spec_complete\" != true ]]; then\n        RULE_STATUS=\"pass\"\n        if [[ -n \"$status_value\" ]]; then\n            RULE_MESSAGE=\"Spec status is '$status_value', not Complete; scaffold markers are allowed\"\n        else\n            RULE_MESSAGE=\"Spec status does not claim Complete; scaffold markers are allowed\"\n        fi\n        return\n    fi\n\n    # A v2.3 spec.md is scaffolded the same way as the docs above, so its own\n    # frontmatter is read too. An older spec.md keeps the verdict it always had.\n    if [[ -f \"$spec_file\" ]] && speckit_carries_token_gate_stamp \"$spec_file\"; then\n        files=(\"spec.md\" \"${files[@]}\")\n    fi\n\n    for file in \"${files[@]}\"; do\n        local filepath=\"$folder/$file\"\n        [[ ! -f \"$filepath\" ]] && continue\n\n        # Skip: scratch/, memory/, templates/\n        if [[ \"$filepath\" == *\"/scratch/\"* ]] || \\\n           [[ \"$filepath\" == *\"/memory/\"* ]] || \\\n           [[ \"$filepath\" == *\"/templates/\"* ]]; then\n            continue\n        fi\n\n        if type -t should_skip_path &>/dev/null; then\n            if should_skip_path \"$filepath\"; then\n                continue\n            fi\n        fi\n\n        local frontmatter\n        frontmatter=$(awk '\n            NR == 1 && $0 == \"---\" { in_frontmatter = 1; next }\n            in_frontmatter && $0 == \"---\" { exit }\n            in_frontmatter { print NR \":\" $0 }\n        ' \"$filepath\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n\n        while IFS= read -r match; do\n            if [[ -n \"$match\" ]]; then\n                local linenum=\"${match%%:*}\"\n                found_markers+=(\"$file:$linenum: title contains [template:\")\n            fi\n        done < <(printf '%s\\n' \"$frontmatter\" | grep -E '^[0-9]+:[[:space:]]*title:[^#]*\\[template:' 2>/dev/null || true)\n\n        while IFS= read -r match; do\n            if [[ -n \"$match\" ]]; then\n                local linenum=\"${match%%:*}\"\n                found_markers+=(\"$file:$linenum: packet_pointer starts with \\\"scaffold/\\\"\")\n            fi\n        done < <(printf '%s\\n' \"$frontmatter\" | grep -E \"^[0-9]+:[[:space:]]*packet_pointer:[[:space:]]*['\\\"]?scaffold/\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n\n        # An authorship string is a weak proxy for \"never edited\": it reports a\n        # fully authored document whose only stale field is the author, and it is\n        # cleared by editing that one field rather than by doing the work. The\n        # scaffold's own placeholder instructions are the durable signal — they\n        # say what has not been filled in, and they go away only when it is.\n        while IFS= read -r match; do\n            if [[ -n \"$match\" ]]; then\n                local linenum=\"${match%%:*}\"\n                local text=\"${match#*:}\"\n                found_markers+=(\"$file:$linenum: continuity still holds a scaffold placeholder:${text}\")\n            fi\n        done < <(printf '%s\\n' \"$frontmatter\" | grep -E \"^[0-9]+:[[:space:]]*(recent_action:[[:space:]]*['\\\"]?Initiali[sz]ed?[[:space:]]|next_safe_action:[[:space:]]*['\\\"]?Replace[[:space:]])\" 2>/dev/null || true)\n\n    done\n\n    # Deduplicate (bash 3.2 compatible)\n    local -a unique_markers=()\n    local seen_list=\"\"\n    if [[ ${#found_markers[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"dcc728","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
