nded Level\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"spec.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Critical Dependencies\",\n+        \"name\": \"Key Decisions\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"spec.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Status Draft\",\n+        \"name\": \"Critical Dependencies\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"spec.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Problem Statement\",\n+        \"name\": \"Problem Statement Callers\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"spec.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"In Scope\",\n+        \"name\": \"Purpose Give\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"spec.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n@@ -121,25 +129,25 @@\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Clean Architecture\",\n+        \"name\": \"Overview Change\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"plan.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Key Components\",\n+        \"name\": \"Pattern Single\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"plan.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Data Flow\",\n+        \"name\": \"Key Components\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"plan.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Current Role\",\n+        \"name\": \"Data Flow Arguments\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"plan.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n@@ -157,25 +165,19 @@\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Recommended Level\",\n-        \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n-        \"path\": \"tasks.md\",\n-        \"source\": \"derived\"\n-      },\n-      {\n         \"name\": \"Completion Criteria\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"tasks.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Verification Checklist\",\n+        \"name\": \"Decision Records\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"tasks.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       },\n       {\n-        \"name\": \"Verification Protocol\",\n+        \"name\": \"Execution Protocol\",\n         \"kind\": \"proper_noun\",\n         \"path\": \"tasks.md\",\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n@@ -187,9 +189,9 @@\n         \"source\": \"derived\"\n       }\n     ],\n-    \"causal_summary\": \"[YOURVALUEHERE: What is broken, missing, or inefficient? 2-3 sentences describing the specific pain point.]\",\n+    \"causal_summary\": \"Callers that need only the level must parse a 16-line report to read one number\",\n     \"created_at\": \"2026-10-26T14:18:27Z\",\n-    \"last_save_at\": \"2026-10-26T14:18:27.899Z\",\n+    \"last_save_at\": \"2026-10-26T14:21:54.743Z\",\n     \"save_lineage\": \"graph_only\",\n     \"last_accessed_at\": null,\n     \"source_docs\": [\n@@ -199,13 +201,13 @@\n       \"acceptance-criteria.md\",\n       \"implementation-summary.md\"\n     ],\n-    \"source_fingerprint\": \"sha256:54948d0afc5a0cb6a883cbd5ac26a7e76021a4b26380789c87c48328f544a546\",\n+    \"source_fingerprint\": \"sha256:2fa82f2378622d0692ab329de538cdf7669fbf2d9ffe860b1f4ad4084ec88821\",\n     \"source_fingerprint_docset\": 3,\n     \"source_doc_hashes\": {\n-      \"spec.md\": \"5db7b388f2085393f1526761d70cbe292aead18b0294ccf8dfc311ef8f159dc8\",\n-      \"plan.md\": \"143c9b6148bf455c5f021521f967a7219dacf1babef960163b10d4d3b5231fb4\",\n-      \"tasks.md\": \"bdccd0c30abb09edaa21eaeccd5756cd9175713907334bc9c1edbbbf75787441\",\n-      \"implementation-summary.md\": \"8fa1824bf8da1f377c3f991ff68a9c706b878109478d543dddc981a959d9c6bd\"\n+      \"spec.md\": \"425e0e90d85cc4b7f70824621e9926799f61bafcbadefa62592542c44164d1a1\",\n+      \"plan.md\": \"9d3000c0e020d3110668e2a2f1550ae613c4eb82734ffbbf800ac7a66543e5f1\",\n+      \"tasks.md\": \"025fb476341dc052567f538a3982afe34ab93ecac9001957c975bcacb5288acf\",\n+      \"implementation-summary.md\": \"0cd7da386560217ee338cb245097740f7f4e797e065c798c1e64a463dd705bf3\"\n     },\n     \"last_active_at\": null\n   }\ndiff -ru /tmp/speckit-before/implementation-summary.md specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md\n--- /tmp/speckit-before/implementation-summary.md\t2026-10-26 15:21:53\n+++ specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/implementation-summary.md\t2026-10-26 15:21:54\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@\n contextType: \"general\"\n _memory:\n   continuity:\n-    packet_pointer: \"scaffold/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\"\n+    packet_pointer: \"zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag\"\n     last_updated_at: \"2026-10-26T14:18:27Z\"\n     last_updated_by: \"template-author\"\n     recent_action: \"Initialized Level 3 template\"\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"3dc05b","exit_code":1,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_5a582c8f07a54587b9e5a4e40a3a51f6","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"// different ceiling, so a longer source produces a fuller causal_summary while the description\n// stays terse.\nexport const SYNOPSIS_FIELD_LIMITS: Record<SynopsisField, number> = {\n  description: 150,\n  causal_summary: 600,\n};\n\nconst OVERVIEW_SECTION_RE = /###\\s+Overview\\s*\\n([\\s\\S]*?)(?:\\n###|\\n##|\\n<!--|$)/i;\nconst PROBLEM_HEADING_RE =\n  /^#{1,4}\\s+(problem\\s+(statement|&\\s*purpose|and\\s+purpose)|purpose)/i;\nconst FRONTMATTER_DESCRIPTION_RE = /^\\s*description:\\s*(.+?)\\s*$/im;\nconst TEMPLATE_STAMP_RE = /^\\s*<!--\\s*SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE:[^|>]*\\|\\s*v(\\d+)\\.(\\d+)\\s*-->/u;\nconst CLAUSE_END_RE = /[,;:](?=\\s)/g;\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. HELPERS\n=== repair description handling ===\n67://   GRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE is structural and included, because the re-derive\n85:// The subset a re-derive can actually settle, because they are assertions about\n86:// graph-metadata.json itself. The others describe description.json contents and\n87:// in-document reference paths, which a re-derive does not write; planning one\n121:// exit code counts it. Carries no apply(): the re-derive is a child process the\n123:const REDERIVE_STEP = Object.freeze({ what: 're-derive graph metadata' });\n241:const REWRITE_TARGETS = ['description.json', 'graph-metadata.json', ...DOCS];\n248:// Measured set: the packet files the re-derive child opened through planted links. Mirrors the packet document lists of the graph parser, the drift check and folder discovery.\n259:  'description.json',\n347:  const file = path.join(folder, 'description.json');\n411:  const description = path.join(folder, 'description.json');\n435:  // not one, and a re-derive computes null. The graph merge keeps a stored\n436:  // parent over a null re-derive and flags it for review, so after a move the\n445:      // A graph file that cannot be read is the re-derive's to report.\n514:  // re-derive is part of the repair rather than a follow-up; skipping it swaps\n519:  // re-derive into a packet whose graph file is a link would replace the link with a\n520:  // regular file. A linked graph file is therefore never re-derived, and the dry run\n550:    // A link among the re-derive's inputs is refused here, whether it was present at planning or\n555:    if (reason && !failure) failure = `re-derive: ${reason}`;\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"e44188","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_5e1e38c2c68a435787528bce16b8b995","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: Spec Authoring Card\ndescription: The short path a model follows to write one spec packet that passes strict validation with no unfilled tokens.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"spec authoring card\"\n  - \"write a spec packet\"\n  - \"spec folder authoring steps\"\n  - \"fill a spec scaffold\"\nimportance_tier: important\ncontextType: implementation\nversion: 1.0.3.0\n---\n\n# Spec Authoring Card\n\nThis card is the short path. Follow the steps in order. Each step has one action, one acceptance line and one command. When the command prints what the acceptance line says, go to the next step.\n\n`references/templates/template-guide.md` is the long guide. Read it only when a section's fill note leaves you unsure what to write.\n\n## 1. BOUNDS\n\nYou write one packet, in one folder. The folder is the one `create.sh` prints.\n\nAllowed writes: the packet folder and its `scratch/` folder.\nForbidden: `git commit`, `git push`, `git checkout`, `git switch`, `git branch`, `git reset`, `git stash`, `generate-context.js`, `/speckit:save`. Do not edit `.skilled/`, another packet or a source file. Do not run `create.sh` twice.\n\nAcceptance: you can name the packet folder and the one command you will run to check it.\nVerify: `pwd` prints the repository root, and `ls <packet folder>` lists `spec.md`.\n\n## 2. PICK THE LEVEL\n\nRun the level helper first.\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/recommend-level.sh --loc <lines> --files <count>\n```\n\nUse the level it prints. If it prints Level 0, use `--level 1`. Do not raise the level yourself. The level decides which files the packet needs.\n\n| Level | Files the packet needs |\n|-------|------------------------|\n| 1 | `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, and `implementation-summary.md` once implementation starts |\n| 2 | the Level 1 files plus `acceptance-criteria.md` |\n| 3 | the Level 2 files plus the architecture sections and a decision record when one is written |\n\nAcceptance: the level in the scaffold header matches the level the helper printed.\nVerify: `rg -n 'SPECKIT_LEVEL' <packet folder>/spec.md` prints one line with that level.\n\n## 3. SCAFFOLD\n\nCreate the packet with one command. Keep `--skip-branch` so no git state changes.\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/create.sh --skip-branch --with-goal --level <level> --track <track> --short-name <two-to-four-words> \"<one sentence>\"\n```\n\nThe command prints the folder it made. Use that path for every later command. When `specs/<track>/graph-metadata.json` exists, `create.sh` also adds the packet to its `children_ids`. That write is the script's, not yours.\n\nAcceptance: the folder holds `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `scratch/`.\nVerify: `ls <packet folder>` lists those names.\n\n## 4. READ BEFORE YOU WRITE\n\nOpen one rendered example at the same level under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/templates/examples/level-<level>/`. Read `spec.md` and `tasks.md`.\n\nDo not copy from a `.tmpl` file. A `.tmpl` file carries tokens and gate markers. The examples are filled and safe to imitate for section shape, not for content.\n\nEach section of your scaffold carries a fill note. The note says what that section needs. Read the note before you write the section. The note is the contract for that section.\n\nAcceptance: you can say, in one sentence, what the first section of `spec.md` must contain.\nVerify: `sed -n '1,40p' <packet folder>/spec.md` shows the fill notes.\n\n## 5. ONE ACTION PER SECTION\n\nEach section does one job. Write one idea per paragraph. Do not repeat the same fact in two sections.\n\n- `spec.md` states the problem, the scope, the requirements and the success criteria.\n- `plan.md` states the approach, the files to change, the test plan and the dependencies.\n- `tasks.md` states the ordered actions.\n- `implementation-summary.md` states what changed and how it was checked. Write it last.\n\nDo not put a task list in `spec.md`. Do not put requirements in `plan.md`.\n\nAcceptance: every heading in the packet has content under it, and no heading holds content that belongs to another heading.\nVerify: `rg -n '^## ' <packet folder>/spec.md <packet folder>/plan.md` lists the headings you filled.\n\n## 6. THE PLAN SHAPE\n\nA plan has 3 or 4 steps. More than 4 steps means the feature is too large for one packet. Stop and ask, as section 11 says.\n\nEach step carries three lines:\n1. What the step does.\n2. The acceptance line: what is true when the step is done.\n3. The verify command: the command a reader runs, and the text it prints.\n\n```markdown\n### Step 1: Add the flag parser\n\nAcceptance: `--quiet` is accepted and the default output is unchanged.\nVerify: `bash script.sh --quiet` prints one line.\n```\n\nAcceptance: `plan.md` holds 3 or 4 steps, and each step has an acceptance line and a verify command.\nVerify: `rg -c '^### Step ' <packet folder>/plan.md` prints 3 or 4.\n\n## 7. TASK LINES\n\nEvery task line has one action, one file and one verify clause.\n\n```markdown\n- [ ] T001 Add the quiet flag to the option parser (`runtime/cli/spec/script.sh`). Verify: `bash runtime/cli/spec/script.sh --quiet` prints one line.\n```\n\nRules:\n- One action per task.\n- Name the file in parentheses.\n- End with `Verify:` and the command plus its expected output.\n- Put the tasks in the order you will run them.\n- Mark a task `[x]` only after its verify command printed the expected output.\n\nAcceptance: every task line, open or done, ends with a `Verify:` clause.\nVerify: `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9].*Verify: ' <packet folder>/tasks.md` and `rg -c '^- \\[[ xB]\\] T[0-9]' <packet folder>/tasks.md` print the same number.\n\n## 8. FILL EVERY TOKEN\n\nA scaffold stamped `v2.3` or later carries tokens. A token starts with `[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:` and ends at the next closing bracket. Replace the whole token, brackets included, with real content. Do not leave a token in a finished packet.\n\nIf you cannot answer a question the token asks, write `UNKNOWN` in its place and write an open question in `goal.md` section 4.\n\nA token in a packet whose `spec.md` says `Status: Draft` is a warning, so strict validation can pass with tokens still in the file. A token in any other status is an error. Do not use the warning as permission. Count the tokens.\n\nAcceptance: the count is 0.\nVerify: `rg -o '\\[YOUR_VALUE_HERE:' <packet folder>/*.md | wc -l` prints 0.\n\n## 9. VALIDATE\n\nRun the validator once, after your last edit, before you claim the packet is done.\n\n```bash\nbash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <packet folder> --strict --quiet\n```\n\nIt prints one `RESULT:` line per packet; the first line is the folder you named, and that line decides. `RESULT: PASSED (errors=0 ...)` is the pass. Do not run it again to re-check a pass.\n\nWhen it prints `FAILED`, run the same command once without `--quiet` and read every failing rule. Fix all of them in one pass, then run the `--quiet` command again. That is one round. Stop after three rounds and write the rules and their errors in the packet's `goal.md`.\n\nWhen the full output contains a `repair-derived.cjs ... --apply` command, run that command, then run the `--quiet` command again. It rewrites generated metadata, frontmatter packet pointers and the Spec Folder row, never your prose.\n\nAcceptance: the `--quiet` command prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\nVerify: the last `--quiet` run printed `RESULT: PASSED`.\n\n## 10. CLOSE\n\nA packet is closeable when:\n- every required file exists for its level\n- every token is filled, or replaced with `UNKNOWN` and an open question in `goal.md`\n- `tasks.md` has no `[B]` line\n- `implementation-summary.md` names the files that changed\n- the section 9 `--quiet` run printed `RESULT: PASSED`\n\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w5963e3680a/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"a52edc","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
